  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and cool weather is expected through the rest of \nthe week, with patchy frost possible across the North Country and \nwestern Southern Tier at times.\n\nAn upper level trough and closed low will slowly move east across \nthe Midwest to Ohio Valley through tonight. The trough will move off \nthe east coast while a coastal low develops late in the week. High \npressure will remain across eastern Canada, bringing dry weather and \ncontinued easterly flow across the eastern Great Lakes though the \nrest of the week. \n\nThe surface high will move further into the region tonight. Clear \nskies and light winds will support favorable radiational cooling \nconditions and result in a cool night. Temperatures in the 30s are \nlikely across the Tug Hill region and portions of the western \nSouthern Tier, which will bring some patchy frost. Low temperatures \nin the low to mid 40s are expected across the lower elevations. \n\nHigh temperatures will gradually increase day to day through Friday.",
